# ─── Last.fm API credentials (local development — OPTIONAL) ──────────────────
# Copy this file to `.env` (gitignored) and paste your own values to build/test
# Last.fm scrobbling locally. `build.rs` reads `.env` and bakes the keys into the
# compile automatically, so you just build normally — no exporting needed.
#
# This is entirely optional. Without a `.env`, the build simply ships
# ListenBrainz-only and the Last.fm "Connect" button reads "not configured in
# this build" — no error, no warning. Official release builds get these from the
# GitHub Actions secrets LASTFM_API_KEY / LASTFM_SHARED_SECRET instead.
#
#   1. Register an app:  https://www.last.fm/api/account/create
#   2. cp .env.example .env      then paste your key + secret below (no quotes).
#   3. Build normally:  cargo run     (or: cargo build --release)
#
# An environment variable already set (shell export / CI secret) always wins, so
# `.env` never overrides one you've set yourself.

LASTFM_API_KEY=
LASTFM_SHARED_SECRET=
